{
  "report_markdown": "# Cap Table \u2014 Cadence\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nModeled 1 scenario(s) for Cadence: 0 full, 0 mixed, 0 repay-only, 1 priced-round terms not set yet.\n1 counsel-review item(s) surfaced. 14 date-sensitive item(s) in watchlist.\n\n> \u26a0 **Cap base was NOT produced by the deterministic spreadsheet mapper.** It was entered\n> manually or extracted from a document (PDF / Carta / pasted), so it was not\n> mechanically verified against a structured source. Confirm each holder and class against\n> whatever these figures came from \u2014 the source document if there was one, or your own\n> share records if you described the cap table in conversation \u2014 before relying on them.\n\n## Current Cap State\n\nAs of: 2026-08-24\n\n| Holder | Shares (as-converted) | % of FD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Maya Gold | 4,000,000 | 44.4% |\n| Ofer Tal | 4,000,000 | 44.4% |\n| Options available | 1,000,000 | 11.1% |\n| **Total fully-diluted** | **9,000,000** | **100.0%** |\n\nOutstanding SAFEs: 1\nOutstanding convertible notes: 1\n\n## Scenarios Modeled\n\n### Cap-implied SAFE snapshot (pre-financing) (SAFE conversion)\n\n**Stage:** Structure only \u2014 no priced round yet (`structural_only`)\n_Cap-implied: the ownership each SAFE locks in from its valuation cap, before a priced round sets the actual share price._\n\n**Cap-implied ownership (pre-financing):**\n- Angel Alice (`safe_001`): 3.1% cap-implied (SAFE price $0.8889, 281,250 shares)\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n## Counsel Review Required\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/)** (`delaware_cross_border.qsbs_date_sensitive`)\n  - US QSBS eligibility and exclusion amounts are date-sensitive and changed for stock issued after July 4, 2025 under OBBBA; cap-table scripts should flag issue date and tax counsel review.\n\n## Date-Sensitive Watchlist\n\n_2 rule(s) to watch (from 2 matched instances)._\n\n| Rule | Status | When | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the stock issue date for this instance. |\n| [Qualified financing threshold and automatic conversion](https://www.cooleygo.com/convertible-debt/) | unknown | \u2014 | Set a benchmark reference date in your inputs to use current data. |\n\n### For-Reference Annotations\n\n_12 item(s) \u2014 rules that don't apply to this engagement in its current state (different jurisdiction, no grants, etc.) but are tracked in case the engagement evolves. No action needed today._\n\n## Sources Cited\n\n- `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`\n\n---\n\n## Coaching Commentary\n\n**Where things stand.** The scenario modeled here \u2014 \"Cap-implied SAFE snapshot (pre-financing)\" \u2014 is structure only, meaning no priced round has been specified yet. That is not a gap in the analysis; it reflects exactly where you are: two SAFEs are outstanding, and the conversion math is ready to run the moment you put a round on the table. What the report shows right now is the cap structure those SAFEs sit inside \u2014 the denominator they will use when they do convert.\n\n**Before the math can finish, two instrument details need your confirmation.** Both SAFEs were extracted at medium confidence, and two fields are still marked as pending your input. Until those are confirmed, the cap-implied price and share counts are held \u2014 the engine does not fill in numbers it isn't sure about. Check the \"Instruments\" section of the report for the specific fields flagged, correct them in chat if anything looks wrong, and the conversion math will complete from there.\n\n**The one item for your counsel's attention: QSBS eligibility (IRC \u00a71202).** Your company is a Delaware corporation, and under the One Big Beautiful Budget Act (Public Law 119-21, \u00a770431, enacted July 4, 2025), the QSBS gain exclusion rules were updated for stock acquired after July 4, 2025. Whether your founder shares, and any shares issued through SAFE conversions, fall under the pre-OBBBA or post-OBBBA rules depends on the exact issuance dates \u2014 which is a facts-and-circumstances determination your tax counsel needs to make, not something the cap-table math can conclude on your behalf. This is worth a short conversation with counsel before you close a round, because the applicable exclusion percentage and holding-period clock can differ materially between the two regimes. Rule reference: `delaware_cross_border.qsbs_date_sensitive`.\n\n**Eleven event dates are missing from the instruments.** The date-sensitive watchlist \u2014 which tracks QSBS clocks, SAFE issuance windows, and other time-sensitive items \u2014 shows 11 instruments or fields where no date was recorded. Two items are already tracked as in-window (meaning their dates are known and the clock is running). For the other 11, the watchlist cannot assess timing status without the dates. The most common missing date in a SAFE stack is the issuance date on each instrument \u2014 if you have the signed documents, pulling those dates now means you'll have a complete picture of where each SAFE sits relative to any applicable holding-period or eligibility clock.\n\n**What to do next.** Confirm the two outstanding instrument fields, supply any missing issuance dates you have, and then add a priced-round scenario when you're ready to see the dilution math. Once a round is on the table \u2014 pre-money, new money, and whether you're topping up the option pool \u2014 the engine will produce full post-financing ownership percentages, the Founder Impact Lens, and a complete counsel packet. Everything else is already in place.\n\n---\n\n*Generated by [founder skills](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills) by [lool ventures](https://lool.vc) \u2014 Cap Table Agent \u00b7 [Share feedback](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills/discussions/new?category=ideas-feedback)*\n",
